      "id": 52651,
      "name": "EvanDan55",
      "username": "EvanDan55",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/{size}/2374_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-01-30T19:48:10.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Iron Legacy is quite possibly the single hardest villain to beat in the game.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>People have been saying that, but I'm not sure. I'd really like him to be the hardest villain to date. Maybe it's because I played early builds of him and haven't played the final build, but The Organization still seemed like the harder foe. But I'm not denying he's really challenging. His advanced mode certainly is the most difficult thing ever.</p>\n<p>Chances are once I get my hard copy of ST and play the final build of Iron Legacy, I'll come back here and agree with everyone that he's the hardest. I mean, I could do it now, but I don't feel like printing the cards again and such. I'd rather wait.</p>",
